1
00:00:03,550 --> 00:00:05,933
Mempire's whole account layer is Mera.

2
00:00:05,953 --> 00:00:07,550
Watch a new player sign up:

3
00:00:07,683 --> 00:00:09,776
one passkey prompt, and that is the

4
00:00:09,796 --> 00:00:10,766
account.

5
00:00:17,050 --> 00:00:20,049
The passkey's PRF output becomes the key,

6
00:00:20,069 --> 00:00:22,037
inside a Mera signing session.

7
00:00:22,483 --> 00:00:24,646
No seed phrase, no extension,

8
00:00:24,666 --> 00:00:26,077
nothing secret stored.

9
00:00:26,338 --> 00:00:28,025
The starter deck lands on chain in

10
00:00:28,045 --> 00:00:29,653
about ten seconds.

11
00:00:30,253 --> 00:00:33,066
The same passkey-derived account signs real Monad

12
00:00:33,086 --> 00:00:34,183
transactions:

13
00:00:34,258 --> 00:00:36,201
here, minting a fighter at its live

14
00:00:36,221 --> 00:00:37,330
Pyth price.

15
00:00:40,253 --> 00:00:41,406
In a staked match,

16
00:00:41,426 --> 00:00:44,169
a per-match session key signs every card,

17
00:00:44,189 --> 00:00:45,783
so a whole battle runs without a

18
00:00:45,803 --> 00:00:47,562
single wallet popup.

19
00:00:53,753 --> 00:00:56,705
And Monad itself verifies a passkey signature,

20
00:00:56,725 --> 00:00:59,201
through its P-256 precompile,

21
00:00:59,221 --> 00:01:01,666
with a tampered copy refused.
